# VCIssuer environment — copy to `.env` for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT and fill in.
#
#   cp rust/.env.example rust/.env      # then `cargo run` from ./rust
#
# The issuer loads `.env` from the current working directory (or the path in VCISSUER_DOTENV) at
# startup. The PROCESS ENVIRONMENT ALWAYS WINS: any variable already set in the environment (e.g. the
# launchd plist EnvironmentVariables on the deployed host, or an `export` in your shell) overrides the
# value here. So a `.env` cannot shadow a trust anchor set by the operator. `.env` is gitignored;
# never commit real secrets — commit only this `.env.example`.
#
# In PRODUCTION do NOT use `.env`: set these in
# deploy/macos/systems.advatar.vcissuer.plist -> EnvironmentVariables (on the host).

# --- Core ---
ISSUER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://issuer.advatar.systems

# --- Trust anchors (hex) ---
# TLSNotary notary public key (SEC1 P-256, hex) — required.
TLSN_TRUSTED_NOTARY_KEY=
# Optional ML-DSA-65 notary public key (raw, hex): set ⇒ TLSNotary artifacts must be hybrid (PQ).
# TLSN_TRUSTED_NOTARY_PQ_KEY=
# Optional trusted eMRTD-reader / liveness backend key (SEC1 P-256, hex). Absent ⇒ NFC-PID disabled.
# EMRTD_TRUSTED_READER_KEY=

# --- Experimental hybrid-PQ credential profile ---
# ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_HYBRID_PQ=true

# --- iProov Service Provider (cross-wallet PID capture liveness) ---
# Same MANDAMUS_IPROOV_* credentials that drive the iProov Web and iOS SDKs. Absent ⇒ capture fails
# closed. Never commit real values.
MANDAMUS_IPROOV_BASE_URL=https://eu.rp.secure.iproov.me/api/v2
MANDAMUS_IPROOV_API_KEY=
MANDAMUS_IPROOV_SECRET=
# MANDAMUS_IPROOV_ASSURANCE_TYPE=genuine_presence
# MANDAMUS_IPROOV_WEB_BASE_URL=wss://eu.rp.secure.iproov.me/ws

# --- PID Capture companion App Clip / universal link (non-secret) ---
# PID_CAPTURE_APP_ID=L2AF8KFX35.eu.advatar.wallet.pidcapture
